SPEC (fill=S): Remove the floating per-target text labels (the sky clutter) but KEEP the in-world diamond bracket (el + frame). Add a right-column CONTACTS panel driven from the global `traffic` array at 10Hz.
Edits:
1. ensureTargetHudPool (@14998): stop creating/appending the tag and readout elements — keep only el + frame. Change the push to `targetHudState.boxes.push({ el })`. (el still gets .target-bracket + child .target-frame.)
2. updateTargetHud (@15568-15587): delete the tagText block, the `poolEntry.tag.textContent` write, and the entire readout block (readout.style.display + lastReadoutAt + readout.textContent). Leave all poolEntry.el transform/class/opacity logic intact.
3. Add markup: a new panel <div id="nhud-contacts" class="nhud-panel"> with a header <div class="nhud-cap">NEARBY CONTACTS</div> and a pre-built pool of 4 rows: <div class="nhud-contact" id="nhud-contact-0" style="display:none"><span class="dia">◆</span><span class="cs"></span><span class="ty"></span><span class="ds"></span></div> ... -1 -2 -3. Place it as a child of #hud (P1 positions it under #course-director).
4. Add function updateContactsHUD() (define near flashStatus @15949) with an internal 10Hz gate (module `let _nhudContactsLast=0; const now=performance.now(); if(now-_nhudContactsLast<100)return; _nhudContactsLast=now;`). Build a scratch array (reuse a module-level array, no per-call alloc) of loaded/visible traffic: for each rec in `traffic` where rec.loaded && rec.group.visible, compute dx=rec.group.position.x-plane.pos.x, dz=rec.group.position.z-plane.pos.z, dist=Math.hypot(dx,dz); push {rec,dist}. Sort by dist, take top 4. For each of the 4 rows: if entry present set row.style.display='flex', toggle class 'hostile' = (rec.targetKind==='ufo-saucer'), set .cs textContent = rec.callsign||rec.hudId, .ty = rec.typeLabel||inferTargetTypeLabel(rec.file), .ds = dist>=1000?(dist/1000).toFixed(1)+'KM':Math.round(dist)+'M' — dirty-check each textContent before writing. Hide unused rows via display='none'. Cache the 4 row elements once (lazy) to avoid getElementById churn.
NOTE: contacts uses `traffic` (world positions) not displayTargets (local to updateTargetHud) — decoupled and always in scope.
