2. Bottom-center NEXT CHECKPOINT chip: add <div id="nhud-checkpoint" class="nhud-panel"><span class="nhud-cap">NEXT CP</span><span class="nhud-num" id="nhud-cp-dist">--</span></div> flanked by 4 small icon buttons that reuse existing toggle handlers (waypoint/course toggle→race-btn or a course toggle; target cycle→dispatch 'C'; camera mode→existing cam key; plane cycle→prop-model-btn). Wire nhud-cp-dist from the existing course-director range in updateCourseDirectorHUD (@16110): also write $courseRange's value (or distanceM) to #nhud-cp-dist (dirty-checked). Icon buttons need pointer-events:auto (add inline or class) since #hud is pointer-events:none.
3. COMMS panel (bottom-right, left of radar): restyle #status-msg — KEEP id="status-msg" (all writers @10098/12309/12512/13011/16090/16095/20512 unchanged). Add class nhud-panel nhud-comms; prepend a static waveform strip <div class="nhud-wave"></div> and a CH pill <span class="nhud-cap">CH 1</span> as SIBLINGS wrapping #status-msg, OR wrap #status-msg inside a comms container that holds the wave + pill + the #status-msg line. The latest flashStatus message already lands in #status-msg via updateStatusGuidance (transientStatus @15948-15952) — no new driver needed.
4. Restyle #course-director (2045-2055) and #mp-race-panel (2056-2061): swap their shell classes to `nhud-panel` (drop thin-surface-hud-shell/game-dialog-chrome to kill backdrop-filter — I3) and restyle inner labels with nhud-cap/nhud-num. Keep every id (course-title/course-next/course-range/course-turn/course-alt/course-cue, race-room/race-timer/race-status/race-board) — writers unchanged. is-hidden toggle logic unchanged.
NOTE: after this stage #nhud-legacy should contain only the drop-only readouts (vspeed/aoa/gforce/gear + the 4 chip-wrapper ids). Those stay hidden (mock omits them) but MUST remain present — $vs/$aoa/$gforce/$gear/$headingChip/$aeroChip/$gearChip/$ammoChip writers still fire.
